1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Your AI assistant needs to pay for things. But one bad instruction could drain your wallet.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Watch one payment. The agent pays a 0.5 NEAR invoice to emoi01, inside a max 1, daily 2, whitelist-only policy.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Success. Half a NEAR to the API provider, settled on NEAR testnet. Transaction on screen.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Now the attack. Send 100 NEAR to attacker. Blocked before signing. No transaction, no hash.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Why NEAR? The limits live in a smart contract, and the agent key can call exactly one method. No frontend can bypass that.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Owner control: pause stops spending instantly. A paused attempt is blocked before signing, no transaction sent. Revoke is terminal.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,000
What limit would you set for your AI? Repo on screen. Built at NEAR Hackathon.
